#EMBEDDED_NOTES
#A speed target can be calculated along a path while attempting to remain within specified target limits of lateral and longitudinal acceleration.
#
#One of the most important uses of the control option Speed (Closed loop) Using Path Preview is to produce realistic driving speed schedules reflecting real highway driving performance levels.
#
#In this example, a car maintains its lane position while accelerating and decelerating within limits typical of highway driving. Top speed is subject to a limit that varies along the route, just like with posted speed limits.
#END_EMBEDDED_NOTES

